The goal of the project was to develop a water safety engineering plan for a large metropolitan area. The goal of the plan was to ensure the safety of residents, protect public health, and safeguard the environment from contamination due to human activity. We developed a comprehensive plan that included the following components: 
1. Water monitoring system – a network of sensors and monitoring stations throughout the city to detect any potential issues with water quality or quantity; 
2. Emergency response protocols – protocols for responding to any potential water-related emergencies, such as a chemical spill or a major storm event; 
3. Education programs – educational initiatives aimed at increasing awareness about safe water practices among citizens; 
4. Water conservation strategies – strategies for reducing water usage and promoting efficient use of this resource; 
5. Pollution prevention plans – strategies for preventing contamination of water sources by industrial or agricultural activities; 
6. Flood control systems – plans for mitigating flooding risks by utilizing natural buffers, constructing levees, installing drainage systems, etc.; 
7. Sanitation system upgrades – upgrades to existing sanitation systems such as septic tanks or sewage treatment plants so that they are able to better process human waste safely. In conclusion, this comprehensive plan will ensure the safety of residents while protecting public health and safeguarding the environment

